<section class="dossier-section dossier-section--tint situation-method" aria-labelledby="separation-method-title">
    <div class="dossier-wrap">
        <p class="dossier-eyebrow"><span>04</span> The intervention</p>
        <h2 id="separation-method-title">First understand it. Then close it methodically.</h2>
        <p class="situation-method-intro">The Private Exposure Assessment is the first intervention. I map the exposure across one phone, one computer and the identities and apps that connect them. I diagnose what matters and close urgent paths that I can safely address.</p>
        <div class="method-rows">
            <article class="method-row"><span>01</span><h3>Map</h3><p>I reconstruct the household overlap across devices, identities, apps, shared services and recovery paths.</p></article>
            <article class="method-row"><span>02</span><h3>Close and harden</h3><p>I harden the devices, identities and apps, configure two security keys, replace risky core accounts where necessary, and move essential access and recovery.</p></article>
            <article class="method-row"><span>03</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>I test every completed change, train you and finish the hardening checklist and private dated record.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p class="situation-method-close">Personal Shield completes the intervention. A typical engagement requires one or two working days, depending on the volume of data and apps, the complexity of the account relationships and the threat model.</p>
    </div>
</section>

